<title>POLAND: Polish wheat, rye, barley prices fall at auctions.</title>
<headline>Polish wheat, rye, barley prices fall at auctions.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish wheat, rye and barley prices all fell more than one zloty per quintal at last week's grain auctions, the Agriculture Ministry said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to March 8    previous week    yr/yr change</p>
<p>   Wheat	54.27 zl/q	 55.71 zl/q	  -1.8 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  41.04 zl/q	 42.47 zl/q	  17.1 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     48.26 zl/q	 49.65 zl/q	   0.0 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
